# ABOUTME: Trivy vulnerability scanner ignore list with justifications
# ABOUTME: Documents accepted CVEs after risk assessment

# ============================================================================
# Trivy Ignore File
# ============================================================================
#
# This file documents vulnerabilities that have been assessed and accepted.
# Each entry MUST include a justification explaining why the vulnerability
# is acceptable in this context.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-XXXXX  # Justification for accepting this vulnerability
#
# Review Policy:
#   - Review all entries quarterly
#   - Re-assess when new patches become available
#   - Remove entries when vulnerability is fixed
#
# Severity Guidelines:
#   - CRITICAL: Generally unacceptable, requires immediate fix or strong justification
#   - HIGH: Requires justification, accept only if risk is mitigated
#   - MEDIUM: May accept with justification
#   - LOW: May accept without detailed justification
#
# ============================================================================

# Example entries (remove when adding real vulnerabilities):
#
# CVE-2024-12345  # Alpine package xyz: No patch available, mitigated by firewall
# CVE-2024-67890  # npm package abc: Only affects Windows, container is Linux-only
# CVE-2024-11111  # False positive: Code path not reachable in container environment

# ============================================================================
# Scanner Strategy
# ============================================================================
#
# Trivy (Primary - Blocks Releases):
#   - Scans packages WE CONTROL: Alpine apk, npm, Python packages
#   - Skips Go binaries: Claude Code binary, gh CLI (managed by Anthropic/GitHub)
#   - Configured with skip-files to exclude /home/dev/.local/**, /usr/local/bin/claude, /usr/bin/gh
#
# Grype (Secondary - Visibility Only):
#   - Scans EVERYTHING including Go binaries
#   - Provides visibility into upstream vulnerabilities
#   - Does NOT block releases
#
# Rationale:
#   We cannot patch vulnerabilities in:
#   - Claude Code binary (provided by Anthropic)
#   - GitHub CLI binary (provided by GitHub)
#   - Their embedded Go module dependencies
#
#   These binaries must be updated by their maintainers. We can only:
#   1. Be aware of issues (via Grype reports)
#   2. Inform users about known upstream vulnerabilities
#   3. Update to newer versions when released
#
# ============================================================================
# Accepted Vulnerabilities
# ============================================================================

# No vulnerabilities currently accepted in packages we control.
# When accepting a CVE, add it below with clear justification.
